# Artificial Evolution changes the text of the permanent, not what other effects have made it (CR 612.1, 613.1c; the ruling:
# "if a creature's creature type has been changed by a spell or ability, changing the card's text won't affect or alter the
# new creature type"). Oko's +1 makes Llanowar Elves a plain Elk (a layer 4 effect, after text-changing in layer 3); Artificial
# Evolution then replaces Elk with Goblin in its text, which has no Elk in it, and the Elves stay an Elk. Replacing Elf with
# Goblin first, as artificial-evolution-changes-a-creature-type-in-a-type-line-for-good does, is the positive control: that
# one is in the printed type line and changes.

